[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/frangio/thyme\">Thyme</a> is a new library for typed metaprogramming that supports dependent types and reasoning about metaprograms. It can be used for code generation by quotation and splicing:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thyme</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Thyme</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prelude</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Staged</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`⟨~</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- elaborates to `1 * x * x * x`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Every <code>c : Code α</code> carries a denotation <code>c.den : α</code> that can be reasoned about:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp_eq_pow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">den</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pow_succ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Metaprograms constructed with staging syntax are coherent, meaning that their generated code is definitionally equal to their denotation, so theorems should carry over.</p>\n<p>The type parameter of <code>Code</code> can contain splices, and proofs can be staged as well:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Staged</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`⟨</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Code generation is the only kind of metaprogramming currently supported, but I'm planning to add other primitives such as pattern matching on <code>Code</code>. I'm interested in growing this library to address more of the use cases currently served by Qq for tactic development, but I haven't looked beyond pattern matching yet.</p>\n<p>There may be some rough edges and certainly sparse documentation for the moment, but please do try it out and let me know your thoughts!</p>",
